It is January, and it is very cold.
I am walking home from the bus stop in Copenhagen.
I see a flower shop on the street.
It is bright and warm inside.
I go into the warm shop.
I look at a small, green plant.
A clerk smiles at me.
"Hello," he says.
"Hello," I say.
"I am looking for a plant."
"Is it a gift?" he asks.
"No, it is for my room," I answer.
"It is a really good plant," he says.
"How much does it cost?" I ask.
"It costs fifty-five kroner," he answers.
I pay for my new plant.
He puts the plant down in a paper bag.
"Here you go, here is your bag," he says.
"Thank you very much," I say happily.
I go out into the cold evening.
My little plant makes me very happy.
